+ * NIF results and received messages. Historically any fragment at all forced a
+ * shrinking GC at the next return / NIF call / allocation — for Gleam-compiled
+ * code, which references compound literals in nearly every function, that was
+ * a full copying collection every few instructions. Fragments are perfectly
+ * valid heap memory (the collector copies out of them like anything else), so
+ * fold them only once they are large relative to the heap or in absolute terms.
+ * @param heap the heap
